ing you know these  were for my daughter who was just about  to  have a baby and i wanted her to have  a treat um so she could feel um  special after the birth and it was also  going to be her  35th birthday on the 7th of january and  we were looking forward to christmas and  had plans  um we then after lunch and after that  bit of shopping we  went to the eating project and i  remember sitting in the biome  with a hot chocolate listening to a  string quartet playing christmas carols  and actually i said to my husband this  is absolutely perfect  this was a perfect weekend and the  future  had so much to hold and when we arrived  home  later that evening the police were  waiting for us  um the last thing i absolutely expected  was for the police officer to tell me  that anna was dead i don't  it was just so surreal it just didn't  feel real  um i just couldn't take it in um  i remember phoning my son-in-law who was  absolutely desperate um  so much pain and shock i  had to get there immediately because i  was thinking about my grandson who was  two at the time  the police were so good they assisted me  to  get to my son-in-law and my daughter's  home  and there that's where i stayed for the  next six to eight weeks while we went  through  christmas i had to identify her body  on christmas eve um  and just working with the police on the  investigation  um her funeral was delayed and wasn't  until the 31st of  january we we saw  caroline um incredibly shocking  footage in the introduction to this  interview taken from a dash cam  of a lorry that that showed the driver  of the vehicle that hit anna  travelling at estimated speeds of 130  miles an hour and by the time  he hit anna's car traveling at more than  a hundred  miles per hour  i have i was so so shocked  um when i saw that footage and i still  look at it now  in absolute pure disbelief that anybody  could drive at speeds like that it is  just so  so selfish if that driver had taken  time to consider the possible  consequences  of his driving at speed anna would be  here now  oscar would be here and we would be  living totally different lives  the impact of him hitting anna from  behind  she was killed instantly and that is the  only thing  that gives me any peace is to know that  she did not suffer and that she did not  know what had happened  but when he hit her the force of  his vehicle hitting going into the back  of her car  concertina the car just squashed it  the car was pushed into a ditch but the  impact was so huge  her seat belt mechanism was broken in  three places  and she was then catapulted on the  vehicle  i know that she was dead before she hit  the ground  but i struggle when i see that because  when i see the cars coming to a halt  in that instant i know the accident has  happened and that she's dead  vulnerable lying in the wet road  um and that no matter what anybody was  trying to do to assist her  that she was dead and oscar was dead and  that our lives had changed totally and  completely in that instant  oscar no one yes i was going to say  the actions of that driver have torn  your family apart left you grieving your  daughter  anna's husband uh widowed and her son  henry  who was as you say two at the time and  how is he now  he's he's a remarkable little boy but he  is going to  suffer um he has lost his mother  in the most awful of circumstances he  had  you know he has was having an afternoon  nap and his mother never came home  and a two-year-old having to try and  explain that  and really extinguishing his hope  that his mother is ever going to come  back um  has been one of the hardest things that  i've had to do  and for him it will be an ongoing  experience  um as he develops and his understanding  develops he will need to go  through what's happened time and time  again  to reprocess it to understand it  to know what happened to his mother  um and that is really really tough  yeah incredibly uh tough indeed and  thank you for speaking ab